{
  "name": "crowned crane",
  "kind": "parts",
  "_about": "a grey crowned crane: slender and pale grey, the long pale-grey neck; the black velvet forehead and over it the crown of stiff golden bristles; the bare white cheek patch topped red, the red wattle under the chin; the wing's great white panel, the golden-straw plumes over it and the chestnut secondaries, black primaries; long black legs (2026-11-08) The BILL is two sharp `horn`s (sharp.js): the upper mandible flat underneath with a keel, the lower flat on top, meeting along a crisp commissure in a true point. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints.",
